# Example Rule (reference)

This rule is a REFERENCE for the Cursor rule format. It demonstrates:

- `.mdc` file extension (NOT `.md`) -- distinguishes rule files from arbitrary Markdown.
- YAML frontmatter with three fields:
  - `description` (string): shown in Cursor's rule picker UI.
  - `globs` (string): file pattern; the rule applies when matching files are open.
  - `alwaysApply` (boolean): if `true`, applies to every session regardless of file context.
- Body content: persistent guidance for the AI agent, kept under 50 lines per the `create-rule` spec.

## Installer pattern

Rules ship in the plugin at `cursor-rules-templates/<name>.mdc` but are NOT auto-loaded from there. The optimus host-side installer (M4 `optimus init <project>` step) copies templates into `<project-root>/.cursor/rules/<name>.mdc`. This is the only Cursor-native location for rules; Cursor does NOT have a user-level rules directory.

## What this rule does (in production)

Nothing -- it is a reference. Production rules carry actionable, project-specific guidance such as:

- Always use TypeScript strict mode for `**/*.ts`.
- Prefer functional component patterns for `frontend/**/*.tsx`.
- Reference the local API client for any new backend endpoint.

